  "result": "Excellent! The bulk discount feature is fully implemented and tested. Here's a summary:\n\n## Bulk Discount Implementation\n\n### Feature Details:\n- **Trigger**: Lines with qty \u2265 10 get an additional 2.5% discount\n- **Application Order**: Applied AFTER the line's own discount (explicit or tier-based)\n- **Accounting**: Counted in the `discount` field in `invoiceTotals`\n- **VAT Basis**: VAT is calculated on the amount after BOTH discounts are applied\n\n### Implementation:\n\n**Modified `src/totals.js`:**\n- Updated `invoiceTotals()` to calculate bulk discount for each line with qty \u2265 10\n- Bulk discount = `amountAfterFirstDiscount * 0.025` (2.5%)\n- VAT calculated on: `amountAfterAllDiscounts = lineTotal - firstDiscount - bulkDiscount`\n\n### Example Calculation:\n```\nLine with qty=10, unitPrice=1000, discountPercent=5%, VAT=21%:\n- lineTotal = 10 \u00d7 1000 = 10,000\n- firstDiscount = 10,000 \u00d7 0.05 = 500\n- amountAfterFirst = 9,500\n- bulkDiscount = 9,500 \u00d7 0.025 = 237.5\n- amountAfterAll = 9,262.5\n- VAT = 9,262.5 \u00d7 0.21 = 1,945.125 \u2192 1,945 (rounded)\n- totalDiscount = 500 + 237.5 = 737.5\n```\n\n### Test Coverage:\n- 30 new bulk discount tests in `test/totals.test.js` covering:\n  - Basic bulk discount (qty \u2265 10)\n  - No discount below threshold (qty < 10)\n  - Bulk discount with existing line discounts\n  - Multiple lines with mixed bulk discount eligibility\n  - Bulk discount with different VAT rates (0%, 9%, 21%)\n  - Large quantities and amounts\n  - Edge cases (exact threshold, vouchers, 0% VAT)\n\n### Test Results:\n- **Total tests**: 379 (349 original + 30 new bulk discount tests)\n- **Pass rate**: 100% \u2713",
